<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Golden file for WP2/WP6/WP7 (ERSAD NeTEx export).
  Source: Confluence page 3825765495 "ERSAD Export aus ATLAS", section
  "Beispiel Tavannes (8500100)" (single-station example).

  Adaptations applied vs. the Confluence draft, per plan section 0.2:
  1. Removed <TotalCapacity>42</TotalCapacity> from <Parking> (numberOfPrmPlaces/capacity is not
     available in ATLAS; only booleans are).
  2. Renamed the ParkingArea id suffix from ":parking:1:prm" to ":parkingArea" (canonical suffix
     from plan section 0.2) and removed its <TotalCapacity>2</TotalCapacity>; kept
     <ParkingUserTypes>registeredDisabled</ParkingUserTypes> (the ParkingArea rule: written only
     because prmPlacesAvailable == YES in this example).
  3. Renamed SitePathLink ids from the draft's ad hoc ":path:ref1-quay3" / ":path:ref1-toilet" to
     the canonical ":pathLink:1" / ":pathLink:2" suffix scheme (and their nested
     AccessibilityAssessment ids accordingly).
  4. No separate "prmTsiCompliantStation" element existed in the draft to remove; it is not
     derivable from ATLAS data and is omitted entirely (listed as a known limitation).
  5. Coordinates are already WGS84 decimal degrees in the source; no conversion needed for this
     golden file's literal values (WP3/WP6 still route real data through CoordinateTransformer).
  6. Markdown backslash-escapes ("STOP\_POINT" etc.) introduced by the Confluence-to-markdown
     export were unescaped back to plain XML text/comments.

  Structural note (not an adaptation, an open question for WP6): this example illustrates
  AssistanceService/TicketingService/TicketingEquipment/StopPlaceEntrance structure using
  invented example data, because real Tavannes ATLAS data has no Contact Point, Parking Lot,
  Reference Point or Relation rows. See ersad/fixtures-tavannes.md for the fixture rows needed to
  reproduce this file byte-for-byte.

  WP6 adaptations (StAX writer is the element contract; plan section 0.2 wins over the draft):
  7. Added xmlns:gml / xmlns:siri declarations to the root element (plan WP6 header).
  8. Removed the StopPlace-level <StepFreeAccess> and the StopPlace AccessibilityAssessment
     <Comment> (additionalInformation): the ERSAD model (ErsadStation) has no source for either.
  9. Removed the <TicketingService> opening-hours fields (DayType/Timeband): ATLAS openingHours is
     free text and cannot be mapped to structured validity conditions.
  10. Removed <NumberOfMachines>: ATLAS has no ticket machine count (only a boolean).
  11. Removed <entrances>/<StopPlaceEntrance>: reference points are not part of the ERSAD model;
      they only appear as SitePathLink From/PlaceRef refs.
  12. ParkingArea id changed from ":parkingArea" on the station sloid to
      "<parkingSloid>:parkingArea" (section 0.2: suffix is appended to the entity's own sloid, and
      the station-level id would collide when a station has several parkings).

  WP7 adaptation (supersedes item 5 above):
  13. <Longitude>/<Latitude> updated from the Confluence draft's literal WGS84 values
      (7.20164538962 / 47.21984466031) to 7.20164539670 / 47.21984467076: the real ATLAS
      station's position is stored as LV95 (east=2582049.83754, north=1229906.62316) and converted
      to WGS84 via ch.sbb.atlas.servicepoint.transformer.CoordinateTransformer, per plan section
      0.2 ("always route coordinates through CoordinateTransformer"); the draft's literal WGS84
      values do not exactly round-trip through that transformer (~9e-8 deg longitude, ~1e-8 deg
      latitude drift). See ersad/README-golden.md.

  Handoff plan §8 / schema-validity follow-up (this revision):
  14. (§8.4) Quay AccessVehicleEquipment id suffix renamed ":boarding" -> ":access" everywhere.
  15. (§8.3, known limitation, no longer exported) Removed StopPlace <VisualSignsAvailable>
      (was sourced from visualInfo), Quay <TactileGuidingStrips> (was sourced from
      contrastingAreas) and PathLink <VisualSignsAvailable> (was sourced from contrastingAreas).
      PathLink TactileGuidanceAvailable (tactileVisualMarks) is kept, renamed to its real NeTEx
      name (TactileGuidingStrips does not exist in the schema; see item 17).
  16. (§8.2) The INFORMATION_DESK contact point (sloid :9999) is now exported as a
      <TicketingService> LocalService in <localServices> (id = contact point sloid), not as
      TicketingEquipment in placeEquipments; TICKET_COUNTER (sloid :1234) stays
      <TicketingEquipment>. LocalService/TicketingService has no AccessibilityAssessment or
      InductionLoops field in the XSD (netex_ifopt_localService_version.xsd), so the information
      desk's accessibility data (if any existed for this fixture) cannot be represented and is
      dropped; only <Name> has a real ATLAS source here.
  17. (§8.1) Quay AccessVehicleEquipment rebuilt using real AccessVehicleEquipmentBoardingGroup
      elements (netex_equipmentVehiclePassenger_version.xsd): <Hoist> (boardingDevice
      LIFTS -> true, NO -> false, else omitted) then <Ramp> (RAMPS -> true, NO -> false, else
      omitted), in that XSD order; written only if Hoist or Ramp is present. <RampAvailable> and
      <BoardingHeightAdjustment> do not exist in NeTEx and are removed. Platform
      levelAccessWheelchair now maps to the Quay AccessibilityAssessment limitation
      <LevelAccessIntoVehicle> instead (same true/false/omit value mapping as before).

  xmllint schema-validity fixes (NeTEx_publication.xsd, v2.0):
  18. TicketingEquipment <HearingLoops> renamed to <InductionLoops> (TicketingEquipmentAccessibilityGroup);
      AccessibilityAssessment is not allowed inside Equipment/PassengerEquipment types at all, so the
      TicketingEquipment's own accessibility booleans are used instead: <InductionLoops>,
      <AudioInterfaceAvailable>, <WheelchairSuitable> (XSD order), sourced from the same
      hearingLoop/other-contact-point accessibility fields as before; any field without a direct
      boolean equivalent in TicketingEquipmentAccessibilityGroup is dropped.
  19. AccessibilityAssessment now always starts with mandatory <MobilityImpairedAccess>
      (AccessibilityAssessmentGroup): the WheelchairAccess limitation's value when present,
      "unknown" otherwise (flagged for business review). Within <AccessibilityLimitation> itself,
      <WheelchairAccess> is mandatory first (MobilityLimitationGroup); PathLink has no ATLAS source
      for it, so "unknown" is substituted there too whenever StepFreeAccess/TactileGuidanceAvailable
      is written (same fallback convention, flagged for business review).
  20. StopPlace child order corrected to the Site/SiteElement/StopPlace XSD group sequence:
      Name, PrivateCode, Centroid, Url, PostalAddress, AccessibilityAssessment, placeEquipments,
      localServices, TransportMode, StopPlaceType, quays, pathLinks (Url and AccessibilityAssessment
      both belong to the generic Place/SiteElement groups, before the StopPlace-specific elements).
  21. PostalAddress child order corrected to Town before PostCode (PostalAddressGroup), matching the
      XSD sequence instead of the draft's PostCode/Town order.
  22. SanitaryEquipment: AccessibilityAssessment now written before SanitaryFacilityList
      (SanitaryEquipmentGroup order), not after.
  23. AssistanceService fields reordered to Note (generic EquipmentGroup, "internal use by
      OPERATOR" comment -> assistanceCondition) then AssistanceFacilityList then
      AssistanceAvailability (AssistanceServiceGroup order); TicketingService then follows
      AssistanceService within localServices per LocalServiceFrame ordering.
  24. ParkingArea: <ParkingUserTypes> moved into its own nested <parkingProperties><ParkingProperties>
      element (ParkingPropertiesGroup), which is where the XSD actually places it, instead of
      directly under ParkingArea.
  25. SitePathLink From/To <PlaceRef> no longer carry a version attribute: the referenced places
      (reference points, quays, toilets) are not necessarily present as versioned entities in this
      delivery, and a version="1" attribute triggers a NeTEx keyref constraint that then fails for
      refs to places outside the delivery; omitting version avoids the keyref check per NeTEx
      reference semantics.
-->
<PublicationDelivery xmlns="http://www.netex.org.uk/netex" xmlns:gml="http://www.opengis.net/gml/3.2" xmlns:siri="http://www.siri.org.uk/siri" version="1.0">
